-- title:
--   Conjugate orders agree up to r-power denominators, elementwise
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a,b$ and let $R,R'$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which are orders in the sense of the project predicate `IsOrder`: each contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, has $\mathbb{Q}$-span equal to the whole algebra, and is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Let $r$ be a natural number assumed prime, and $v$ a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose ideal contains the image of $r$. Let $\gamma_0$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ and $g$ a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ whose component at every finite place $w\neq v$, taken via the base change of the evaluation map, equals $1$. Assume moreover that conjugating $R'$ by the unit $(\gamma_0\otimes 1)\cdot g$ gives $R$, where conjugation means: form the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes \alpha$ with $z\in R'$ and $\alpha$ an adele integral at every place, move it by $x\mapsto \beta x\beta^{-1}$, and pull back along $d\mapsto d\otimes 1$. The conclusion is twofold: for every $x\in R$ there is $K\in\mathbb{N}$ with $r^{K}\,\gamma_0^{-1}x\gamma_0\in R'$, and for every $y\in R'$ there is $K\in\mathbb{N}$ with $r^{K}\,\gamma_0 y\gamma_0^{-1}\in R$.
--
--   This is the elementwise form of the local–global dictionary for quaternionic orders: if two orders become conjugate by a finite idele which is trivial outside the single place $v$ above $r$, then the rational conjugation by $\gamma_0$ carries each order into the other after clearing a power of $r$. It is used in the construction of fake elliptic curves with prescribed endomorphisms over the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting, via [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_fakeEllipticCurve_isFormalModuleVia_hasHeight_four_endomorphismDictionary_endIsoFull_of_isUnit_two`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_fakeEllipticCurve_isFormalModuleVia_hasHeight_four_endomorphismDictionary_endIsoFull_of_isUnit_two).
